cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Nhat Nguyet: open source code and data for Zi Wei Dou Shu, BaZi and numerology"
message: "If you use this software or its data, please cite it as below. Credit line: Data: Nhat Nguyet (nhatnguyet.org)."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Nhat Nguyet"
    website: "https://nhatnguyet.org"
version: "0.3.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24358013"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.24358013"
    description: "Concept DOI, resolves to the latest version"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Nhat-Nguyet/nhatnguyet-lunar-ziwei-bazi-numerology"
url: "https://nhatnguyet.org/en/ma-nguon-mo"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  TypeScript and Python libraries, a command line tool, an MCP server and 5
  web components for the Vietnamese lunar calendar (Hanoi time, UTC+7) and
  the Chinese, Korean and Japanese ones, the 24 solar terms, auspicious hours,
  Zi Wei Dou Shu, BaZi, Pythagorean numerology and 206 Vietnamese festivals,
  with an English API and named school options where the books disagree.
  Every result reproduces the engine behind nhatnguyet.org (engine 2.2.0)
  and is checked by 17,291 core test vectors (18,819 including school
  options and auspicious hours). The calendar is checked
  against NASA new moons and IMCCE solar terms from 1900 to 2100; on 2,724
  of those 73,414 days the Vietnamese lunar date differs from
  lunar-javascript. Code is MIT; data, readings and test vectors are CC BY
  4.0.
keywords:
  - zi wei dou shu
  - tu vi
  - bazi
  - four pillars of destiny
  - numerology
  - vietnamese lunar calendar
  - chinese calendar
  - solar terms
  - auspicious hours
  - vietnamese festivals
  - test vectors
  - open data
references:
